\section{Discussion}
The three diameter means are close, with a total spread of about 1\% relative to their overall mean. The plotted points are consistent with a broadly similar coefficient over the tested range, but the measurements do not yet establish a universal or Reynolds-independent coefficient. Each speed and diameter appears to have only one run. Further, cylinder diameter is confounded with measurement date and water temperature: each size was tested in a separate session, and the largest cylinder was not tested under the same load-cell installation as the March cylinder.

The tank cross section is 0.675 m$^2$. If the cylinders span the 0.9 m tank width and are aligned across the flow, the nominal frontal blockage based on $DL$ is approximately 2.3--4.5\%, before support blockage; this estimate depends on geometry not documented in the available notes. Blockage, wall proximity, free-surface effects, end effects, support drag, and the method used to establish towing speed may all affect the inferred coefficient. These need to be documented and assessed before comparison with canonical infinite-cylinder data.

A complete uncertainty analysis should combine calibration-fit uncertainty, baseline drift, force fluctuations over the selected interval, tow-speed uncertainty, dimensional uncertainty, and uncertainty in submerged length. The within-window force standard deviation reported by the processing scripts is not a substitute for independent repeatability. Run 17 was excluded because its raw voltage trace drifted upward by approximately 0.088 V after the initial tare; with no post-run zero measurement available to recover the offset, its mean force is unreliable.

\section{Conclusions}
Tow-tank drag measurements were assembled for 30 runs on three finite circular cylinders. Using the measured water temperature for each run, the Reynolds-number range is approximately $4.7\times10^3$--$5.0\times10^4$. Run 17 was excluded because baseline drift made its tare-corrected force unreliable. The remaining data yield mean coefficients from 1.143 to 1.157 across diameters. A documented uncertainty budget and facility and support corrections remain necessary for a defensible final result.

\section*{Data and code availability}
Raw records, calibration files, run metadata, processing scripts, and the analysis notebook are included in this project. The analysis and figure are managed as project artifacts with Calkit. A final release should include a versioned repository identifier and an archived data record.

